Palimind desktop-native
=======================

This directory vendors the Linux-capable portion of the agent-desktop
project, which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Upstream:
  project:  agent-desktop
  version:  v1.1.0 (commit 17467da5142d471b1e3a6b24828a5d3ad4d8c547)
  source:   https://github.com/agent-desktop/agent-desktop
  license:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)

Vendored crates:
  vendor/agent-desktop/crates/core    (unmodified)
  vendor/agent-desktop/crates/linux   (modified; see patches/ and below)

The `vendor/agent-desktop/skills/` and `vendor/agent-desktop/tests/`
directories are vendored unchanged because the core crate compiles the skill
documents in with `include_str!` and its tests read the fixture corpus.

Local modifications (all marked with `// Palimind:` in the source)
------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/linux/src/system/bus/mod.rs
  Announce the event listener with the one-argument RegisterEvent(s) form
  declared by at-spi2-core 2.44. Upstream sent a three-argument body that the
  installed registry rejects ("invalid signature sass").

crates/linux/src/system/signal/subscription.rs
  Same RegisterEvent(s) correction for the wait subscription path.

crates/linux/src/tree/properties/interface_reads.rs
  Read action names by probing Action.GetName(i) instead of Action.GetActions.
  On at-spi2-core 2.44, GTK3/GTK4 widgets advertise the Action interface while
  their ATK user-data is not an AtkAction; serializing the GetActions reply
  aborts the application. GetName(i) reaches the same names and is safe on the
  measured hosts.

crates/linux/src/tree/properties/node_read.rs
  Thread the corrected action read through the snapshot walk (no behaviour
  change beyond the interface_reads delta).

crates/linux/src/tree/walk/walker_expand.rs
  A compact snapshot no longer descends below a node whose AT-SPI SHOWING bit
  is clear (closed menus, hidden panels, unrealized popups). This is what took
  the calculator snapshot from p95 ~476 ms to ~177 ms. Unknown state is not
  treated as hidden, `find`/`wait` keep their own read purposes, and
  PALIMIND_DESKTOP_PRUNE_OFFSCREEN=0 disables it.

crates/linux/src/system/overlay/cursor_overlay_tests.rs and the
crates/linux/src/system/bus/*_tests.rs, system/launch/launch_window_tests.rs,
tree/observe/node_evidence_tests.rs, tree/properties/interface_reads_tests.rs
  Test fixtures updated for the two changes above, plus a short temporary
  socket path so the fixture fits SUN_LEN from a deep workspace checkout.

No modifications are made to crates/core.

